title: 'ProvenSky: Devlog 001'
date: 2026-11-21
summary: My drone sim and mission planner now have one name. ProvenSky lets you plan routes, test them in a physics sim, then fly.
art: provensky
---

Drone Sim and the Multi-Drone Mission Planner are now one product: **ProvenSky**.

## What it is

- **A sim with real physics.** It's a lightweight virtual drone for running test flights and problems before any hardware leaves the ground.
- **A planner for several drones.** You plan and model routes for more than one drone in one place.
- **Built on what already works.** It's built in Godot, on top of open-source tools, not written from scratch.
- **Made for Canada.** Canadian drone rules are part of the design from day one.

## What's next

- A mobile app that stays in sync with the planner. Easy to use comes first.
- Pulling drone positions out of FPV footage.
- A proper video demo, right here.

Plan → Simulate → Fly.
